title: clipboard:copy
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Generic panel commands]]
kind: reference
summary: Copy a panel's checked files, or the one under its cursor (self / a panel type)

Puts files in the GUI's file clipboard, to be copied where `file-manager:paste` (or a ''Paste'' of a right-click menu) is run: the focused panel's with `self`, the panel type's named otherwise ([[Generic panel commands]]). The files are those of the checked metarecords when some are checked ([[Cross-panel selection]]) — wherever they were checked, in this list or not, a metarecord without a file giving none —, and otherwise the one under the cursor. It works in the [[file-manager panel]] and the [[metarecord-list panel]], which provide `paths`; with no file to copy, it says so and leaves the clipboard as it was.

The clipboard is one for the whole GUI: it is shared with the other workspaces and with the ''Copy'' of every panel's right-click menu ([[Context menus]]). It is the global GUI variable `clipboard` ([[Global GUI variables]]); `clipboard:clear` empties it.
